# Hohes C: one ring of the Operettensaenger's high-C sound column. A flat
# ring seen from slightly above, hollow and at most 5 px tall: thin i back
# arc, a 1 px w front arc with k only below it (reads on light sky and white
# facades). The renderer
# stacks a ring every 8 px and runs alternate rings half a period apart, so
# the column shimmers upwards. Pale and hollow on purpose: no flat top lip
# (not a platform), never gold, no note shapes (the Blasmusiker's).
# ring: frame 0 = the ring at its full 12 px, frame 1 = 1 px higher and
# narrower, with w shock ticks at both sides: stacked rings alternate, so
# the column's edges vibrate.
sprite = hohes_c
size   = 16x8
origin = 8,8
hitbox = 2,0,12,8
anim   = ring frames=2 ticks=4 loop
---
frame ring 0
................
................
................
....iiiiiiii....
..ii........ii..
..kww......wwk..
...kkwwwwwwkk...
.....kkkkkk.....
frame ring 1
................
................
w....iiiiii....w
.w.ii......ii.w.
...kww....wwk...
....kkwwwwkk....
......kkkk......
................
